F11 (source P2, local P2, confirmed) is owned by M152.1. Evidence: removed handleBindFormatting/action in M147.5 versus current web/src/WorkflowStepInspector.tsx, useStepBinding.ts and retained fnct lowering. This restores an explicit supported path, not the old fabricated defaults.

**Outcome.** Let the operator explicitly author the already supported identity and gmail.render_raw steps with real metadata and editable mappings.

**Write set.** web/src/ inspector/binding presentation and component tests, Ramen-owned explicit function metadata/binding adapters and focused backend tests, required internal/gui/static assets and owning memory-bank records. The owner subsequently directed the concrete local remediation: add and qualify a declared function catalog on a local Udon successor to `aff5c2c1e85141b80e407c130a689f7b5d625f3f`, then adopt that exact successor in Ramen. This exception permits the necessary Udon pin update and local commit; it does not authorize other pin changes, remote push or a generic runtime expansion.

**Tasks.**

- **M152.1 — Restore an explicit supported function choice.** Check current fixture/tool readiness, then expose explicit identity and gmail.render_raw selection. Tie function metadata to the retained runtime and compute evidence digests from its declared metadata; fabricate no fallback digest/source/function. Show the chosen function and editable input/output/upstream mappings before binding. Do not infer Gmail formatting from field names or silently supply personal destinations/templates. Validate the selected supported metadata at the backend and preserve exact plan/mapping semantics.
- **M152.2 — Qualify the inspector and backend journey.** Add positive/refusal component and backend coverage for read -> selected formatter -> send using fake data/providers, including missing metadata, invalid function choice and edited mappings. Reuse unchanged retained-runtime evidence only with checked identities. Run full Go checks, required make ui-build and make ui-check with unchanged-lock offline restoration only when ready, relevant affected checks, and reviewed matching embedded assets. Complete docs, task/whole reviews and handoff.

**Acceptance.** Both supported local functions can be explicitly selected and bound from the inspector; mappings remain inspectable/editable. No heuristic selection, fabricated identity, live send or new authority is introduced. Component/backend journey and required embedded-asset qualification pass.

**Verification.** Keep golight budgets and Node>=22.12 policy. The owner separately authorized obtaining the exact locked Vite 8.3.5 and Vitest 5.0.5 packages; both were downloaded into workspace cache and verified against the unchanged lockfile. The owner subsequently approved acquisition of the 15 exact Linux x64 locked transitive tarballs listed in the M152 status manifest, with lockfile integrity verification; no other downloads are added. Subsequent npm ci uses verified existing cache, offline mode and disabled install hooks/audit/update traffic. Missing other payloads block UI gates. Qualify the exact local Udon successor and its catalog offline before Ramen adoption. Run focused DOM/backend tests, GOWORK=off make check, make ui-build, make ui-check and git diff --check; applicable race checks remain required. No physical browser or real provider/model. Required checks, task reviews, a passed
whole review within ten persisted iterations, documentation, downstream
reconciliation and normal retirement precede acceptance. No old attempt or
action quantity transfers. Cheap readiness/focused diagnostics precede each
counted expensive check; preserve the package verification-attempt gate and
record reservations/results separately from review iterations.

**Compatibility/downstream.** Existing saved fnct plans remain readable. This restores the authoring route with explicit evidence and a narrowly scoped declared catalog for the two already supported functions. Kinet W25/W26 follow only by serial priority and gain no dependency on this milestone.

**Authorization requirements (conditions, not permission).** The proposed
combined launch is local only. No publication, push, download, live origin,
sudo, SSH or deployment requirement is scheduled. Its named gates retain
separate bounded allowances only after a future checksum-approved launch.

